@local @local_assistente
Feature: Texts generated by the model are shown as text
  In order not to run markup that comes from a generated text
  As a teacher
  I need the synthesis to be escaped

  Background:
    Given the following "users" exist:
      | username | firstname | lastname | email                | lang |
      | teacher1 | Teacher   | One      | teacher1@example.com | en   |
      | student1 | Student   | One      | student1@example.com | en   |
    And the following "courses" exist:
      | fullname | shortname |
      | Course 1 | C1        |
    And the following "course enrolments" exist:
      | user     | course | role           |
      | teacher1 | C1     | editingteacher |
      | student1 | C1     | student        |

  Scenario: A synthesis with script and bold tags is shown literally
    Given the following "local_assistente > configs" exist:
      | course | enabled |
      | C1     | 1       |
    And the following "local_assistente > syntheses" exist:
      | course | section | content                                      |
      | C1     | 1       | <script>alert(1)</script> and <b>bold</b>    |
    And I log in as "teacher1"
    When I open the "synthesis" tab of the assistant in course "C1"
    Then I should see "<script>alert(1)</script> and <b>bold</b>"
    And "b" "css_element" should not exist in the ".local-assistente-query" "css_element"
